--!strict
--!native
-- Every code and reason jess-save's sources spell, as they spell it: what its reports hold, and
-- so what this package's hold. The list is each string literal of `libs/save/src/*.rs` in jess at
-- the commit before the native tooling went (`ed94500^`) that is made of letters, digits, `_`,
-- `-`, and spaces and has a `_` or a `-` in it, leaving out the tests, comments, serde
-- attributes, and the messages handed to `ok_or`, `expect`, `invalid!`, and `format!`. A code of
-- one lowercase word (`verified`, `blocked`) is spelled the same every way and isn't listed.
--
-- `Unreported` are the two of them no report can hold: `not_target` is the role a record has
-- until it is given its own (`scan.rs`), and `known_removed_dependency_references_remain` is the
-- reason of a verification that failed, which is raised as an error instead (`verify.rs`).
local Unreported = { 'known_removed_dependency_references_remain', 'not_target' }

